  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 5.3. Increased capacity of Member States to design and deliver innovative, flexible and inclusive learning options, encompassing work-based learning and quality apprenticeships</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Kenya through the Ministry of Education and the National Qualification Authority, in consultation with social partners, developed and adopted a gender-responsive Recognition of Prior Learning (RPL) policy and strategy in April 2022, using ILO standards related to Recognition of Prior Learning (RPL) and the mutual recognition of qualifications With support from the Netherlands, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs funded Inclusive jobs and education for refugees and host communities (PROSPECTS) in Kenya (KEN/19/51/NLD), the ILO provided technical support for the development and adoption of the RPL policy which was approved by the Cabinet in April 2022. The support included the development of the RPL policy framework, implementation guidelines and tools, establishment of the National Implementation Committee and National Advisory Committee, training 52 Recognition of Prior Learning (RPL) practitioners (assessors, verifiers, and counsellors), in April and May 2022 on RPL methodology and assessment to facilitate an extended RPL pilot in Kenya that benefited 324 RPL candidates. From March 2022 to June 2023, the ILO in collaboration with Kenya National Qualifications Authority (KNQA), supported the determination of a differentiated unit cost model for RPL assessments. The costing model has been finalized, awaiting validation and gazettement.</narrative>
   </description>
